    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Jackson Merrill** is our premier play, benefiting from a +13% platoon edge against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez and a favorable matchup against a pitcher with slow delivery, which optimizes his stolen base potential. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Nasim Nunez** (71.66) benefit immensely from the wind-out conditions and a high-exposure matchup against Michael Lorenzen. While **Nasim Nunez** is batting ninth, his versatility and the 19% boost from Lorenzen\u2019s SP skill profile make him a sneaky high-floor play despite the bottom-of-the-order penalty. **Cole Carrigg** (71.23) also finds himself in an elite spot, leveraging a combination of park factors and the favorable wind to maintain his utility as a speed-first asset.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involves the bench, where **Miguel Vargas** (55.79) narrowly missed the final lineup spot. While **Miguel Vargas** possesses an impressive xwOBA of 0.399 and benefits from Kumar Rocker\u2019s slow delivery, the optimizer favored **Sam Antonacci** (59.41) due to **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s assumed leadoff role and the specific platoon efficiency against Rocker. We are also monitoring **Kyle Tucker** (57.32), who presents a lower score than usual due to facing the formidable Zack Wheeler; he remains a start based on his pedigree, but he is the most vulnerable member of the outfield if our late-breaking lineup data suggests a defensive rest day.\n\nManagers must remain vigilant regarding the 33% rain risk at the venue hosting **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Cole Carrigg**. While the metrics for **Curtis Mead** remain strong (63.58) thanks to his platoon and park advantages, the volatility of weather in that specific stadium adds a layer of risk. All projected lineup positions remain \"Lineup Pending\"; should the actual orders shift\u2014particularly regarding **Drake Baldwin** or **Jacob Wilson**\u2014we will re-evaluate the utility of our bench options like **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jorge Polanco**, who are currently waiting in the wings should any starters be scratched.",
